GLM-5.3-Flash from an EXL3 pack on one GPU (TF_GLM_RANK=0, TF_GLM_WORLD=1), and faster EXL3 prompt experts.

What:
- cuda_weights.zig: an EXL3 checkpoint (config quant_method exl3) loads through core/exl3_load: KDA [q|k|v] and o, DSA
  q_a, kv_a, q_b, o and the indexer's wq_b, the dense MLPs, the routed experts with the shared expert stacked last (the
  router's shared slot, weight 1), eh_proj and the head as EXL3 groups; the small fp16 matrices (f_a, g_a, b, f_b, g_b,
  kv_b, router, indexer wk/weights_proj/gate/k_norm) as bf16; the fused conv1d. Pages are released layer by layer.
- cuda_mat.zig: a projection is bf16 or EXL3 (`Mat`), one matmul for both; blocks keep EXL3 projections apart and copy
  their rows into place (KDA's [q|k|v|f_a|g_a|b] rows) or read them at their own stride (DSA's q_a and kv_a).
- cuda_moe.zig: EXL3 experts run every slot through exl3_experts.run into fp32 rows (2048 rows a call).
- cuda_forward.zig: the head and MTP's eh_proj through `Mat`; MTP drafts through the EXL3 head (no BF16 head to make the
  4-bit draft head from); one rank skips the pieced exchanges. cuda_engine.zig: EXL3 configs skip the ModelOpt check and
  load the EXL3 kernels; more than one rank is refused for EXL3. qlinear: decodeF32/promptF32 for EXL3.
- exl3_experts: prompt rows (256+) take a 64-column x 64-member program that decodes each weight tile once for four
  16-row member tiles, over a device work list of the member groups that exist (the old grid launched ~2.4M programs a
  projection at 2048 rows, ~94% of them empty). A row's arithmetic and order are unchanged; decode rows keep the old shape.
Why: one DGX Spark holds GLM-5.3-Flash only as EXL3 (turboderp/GLM-5.3-Flash-exl3 2.05bpw: 2-bit experts, 3-5 bit
elsewhere, 80 GiB); 1.0.12 serves the family only from NVIDIA's 190 GiB NVFP4 checkpoint over several hosts.
Verified: `tf-cuda-test exl3` (all pass after the kernel change); served greedy replies identical drafted vs
`"draft": false`, concurrent vs solo, and before vs after the experts change (sha 570d68a56234); prefill 424 -> 493 tok/s.

